 → `hide_from_taskbar(WS_EX_TOOLWINDOW)` → `start_screen_share_monitor()` → `SetWindowPos(HWND_TOPMOST)` → start hotkey listener thread\n- **IPC weakness**: Hotkeys write JSON to `%TEMP%\\spectra_command.json`, polled every 200ms by `GlobalCommandMonitor` in `src/commands.py`. This leaves filesystem artifacts.\n- **Screenshot weakness**: Frontend uses `navigator.mediaDevices.getDisplayMedia()` which triggers OS screen-sharing banners\n- **Hotkey library**: `pynput.keyboard.GlobalHotKeys` + `Listener` in daemon thread\n- **Screen share monitor**: `EnumWindows` loop scanning 40+ indicator titles and 25+ window classes every 1.0s\n- **Process disguise**: `launcher.cs` copies `python.exe` to `WinSysHost.exe`\n\n### C# Transparency Failure Analysis (for reference — abandoned)\n- `SetLayeredWindowAttributes` does NOT affect WebView2 child HWNDs (airspace problem)\n- `AllowsTransparency=\"True\"` in WPF also breaks WebView2\n- WPF `Window.Opacity` via DWM composition should theoretically work but didn't produce visible results\n- Low-level keyboard hooks (`WH_KEYBOARD_LL`) get killed by Windows if callback takes >300ms — must use `ThreadPool.QueueUserWorkItem` + `Dispatcher.BeginInvoke`\n- Delegate for hooks must be pinned with `GCHandle.Alloc` to prevent GC collection\n\n### Visual Issues Found (from research)\n- 30+ emoji instances across HTML and JS dynamic content\n- 5+ runtime `<style>` injections from JS files (live-interview.js, preset-manager.js, screenshot-service.js)\n- Infinite `@keyframes pulse` animations in live-interview.css\n- Neon gradients on Start Interview button (`linear-gradient(135deg, #34d399, #10b981)` + glow box-shadow)\n- Staggered 20ms list item animations in markdown-styles.css\n- Neon cyan `::selection` color and link colors\n- Brand naming inconsistency: \"Aura\" appears in title, preflight heading, hotkeys.js, main.js\n\n---\n\n## 5. Files and Code\n\n### Edited Files\n- `web/index.html` — Removed all emojis (~15), fixed Aura→Spectra naming,